      },
      "graph_node": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.SemigroupDecay.forced_exponential_decay_of_scaled_dissipation_from",
      "reconstruction": {
        "text": "Let q, λ, F ∈ ℝ, with λ > 0. Let E,D : ℝ → ℝ form a dissipation curve with scale q: E is continuous, and for every u ∈ ℝ the right-sided derivative of E at u (within [u,∞)) exists and equals -qD(u). Assume that λE(u) ≤ qD(u) + F for every u ∈ ℝ. Then, for every s,t ∈ ℝ with s ≤ t, E(t) ≤ E(s) exp(-λ(t-s)) + (F/λ)(1-exp(-λ(t-s))).",
